WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.067
Step nine assembles the
period for the ISSO,

2
00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:06.587
from the twenty-eighth to
the thirtieth of October.

3
00:00:06.587 --> 00:00:10.505
Two packages, no chain breaks,
no audit coverage gaps,

4
00:00:10.505 --> 00:00:13.238
six incidents, and complete is false.

5
00:00:13.238 --> 00:00:18.903
The summary counts three activations,
two Tier 0 and one Tier 1; four requests,

6
00:00:18.903 --> 00:00:24.838
two approved and one denied; and one Tier
0 or Tier 1 activation without approval.

7
00:00:24.838 --> 00:00:26.450
Then the Gate 4 table.

8
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.501
Residual standing privilege:

9
00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:33.012
one on the exceptions list with a
reason, eight outside it, so not met.

10
00:00:33.012 --> 00:00:36.073
Evidence for every
elevation in the period:

11
00:00:36.073 --> 00:00:39.388
not met, because one
activation had no approval.

12
00:00:39.388 --> 00:00:43.767
Whether the exception register is
current, and whether the access-related

13
00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:48.288
group policy settings are retired, are
left to people: not decided by this code.

14
00:00:48.288 --> 00:00:50.013
The period exits with two.

15
00:00:50.013 --> 00:00:53.125
Object I D's only; the
packages hold the names,

16
00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:56.210
under the evidence store's access control.
